              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "tt_qhTemperature",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 64.699999809265,
              "coords": {
                "tt_quarter_hour_rows": 94
              },
              "tolerance": {
                "rel": 1e-12
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "the_recurrence_is_anchored_to_hour_1_step_1",
          "description": "`firstQHTankTemperature` is the hour-1 step-1 quarter-hour temperature, selected by KEY. It is the additive anchor of every one of the 96 cells -- `1.4 * sumTempDelta + first` -- so if the key selection picked a different row the whole trajectory would translate and the SHAPE would still look right. It is 63.7999992371, which is `float(63.8)` widened, and it is not 63.8: asserting the rounded decimal at rel 1e-12 would fail, which is the point of carrying the snapshot's twelve digits in the input array.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.0
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "tt_firstTankTemperature",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 63.7999992371,
              "tolerance": {
                "rel": 1e-12
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "TTG_1b_the_recurrence_reproduces_the_reference_tank_temperatures",
          "description": "THIS IS THE RECURRENCE, checked against the reference's own 96-row `QuarterHourTankTemperature` table. Cells 1..6 are the first hour and a half, and cells 93 and 96 are the last hour -- 65.28768 and 64.3096, ninety-odd cells downstream of the anchor, so they are only reachable if every earlier cell was published before the sweep advanced. `esm-spec` §4.3.1.1 point 3 is what makes that true and points 1 and 4 are what forbid the vectorised evaluation that would not. The tolerance is rel 1e-6 because this column is stored at six significant figures: half a unit in the sixth digit of a number just above 10 is 7.9e-07 relative, and the worst of these eight cells is 1.812e-07. Cell 2 equals cell 1 EXACTLY (both 63.8) and that is not a coincidence or a rounding: row 1's carried delta is the anchor subtracted from the temperature it was taken from, so it is exactly zero, and 1.4 * 0 + first is first. A recurrence that had been dropped and laundered would also show 63.8 there -- which is why the assertion that matters is cell 96.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.0
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "tt_qhTankTemperature",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 63.8,
              "coords": {
                "tt_quarter_hour_rows": 1
              },
              "tolerance": {
                "rel": 1e-06
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "tt_qhTankTemperature",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 63.8,
              "coords": {
                "tt_quarter_hour_rows": 2
              },
              "tolerance": {
                "rel": 1e-06
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "tt_qhTankTemperature",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 63.485,
              "coords": {
                "tt_quarter_hour_rows": 3
              },
              "tolerance": {
                "rel": 1e-06
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "tt_qhTankTemperature",
              "time": 0.0,
